A||N||3||Vlad||Cold start injector.||||1||
Z||000000||Vlad||05-01-2001||02:59 AM||||Hello guys,<P>I suspect that my cold start injector is ON all the time. I don't have pressure gauge to test it properly so I was wondering if there is any harm if I disconnect the injector harness for a while and see what happens.<P>Also, what should I ground to what if I test it with a test light ?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||wilburt||05-01-2001||10:36 AM||||I suspected the same thing when my car would run very rich at start-up. Just unplug the harness connector from the top of the CSI. The CSI is 'ON' only while cranking. However, if its stuck open, it'll still let fuel run through. I would try and have ALL the injectors tested if unplugging it dosen't help. Without an injector tester, I'd say replace it with a known good CSI to be sure. My problem was #3, and #4 injectors were leaking.||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||05-01-2001||03:21 PM||||To answer your question, I don't see how disconnecting the CSI could hurt anything (unless you hurt yourself, and/or break a connector!).<P>If you connect a standard 12-volt test light across the terminals of the CSI, it should glow when the CSI is "on."  Polarity doesn't matter, in this case. <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Vlad||05-01-2001||03:34 PM||||Thanks guys.<P>Will give it a try.<P>||||reg||1
